or survived myself, but since you asked :)

If you had first gone downstairs _without_ the naughty kitten, you
would have seen the boulder before finding the trap.  From (painful)
experience I have come to regard any boulder in a room as suspicious
and assume it is pointed right at me.  Then you could have walked over
to the boulder, staying off the orthogonal, and pushed it off of its
rollers.  You also could have waited for a monster to trip the trap,
or at least showed you where to safely walk.

I actually specifically don't bring my pet downstairs with me on my
first >, partially for the reason you observed and also so that I have
first dibs on tripe rations, can go back up if I'm not ready to
explore the Gnomish Mines, or can gain some xp.

